b> are the numbers 0, 1, 2, 3, and so on, possibly excluding 0. The terms <b>positive integers</b>, <b>non-negative integers</b>, <b>whole numbers</b>, and <b>counting numbers</b> are also used. The set of the natural numbers is commonly denoted by a bold <span class=\"texhtml \"><b>N</b></span> or a blackboard bold <span class=\"nowrap\">та<span class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><img src=\"https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/fdf9a96b565ea202d0f4322e9195613fb26a9bed\" class=\"mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"vertical-align:-0.338ex;width:1.678ex;height:2.176ex\" /></span>та</span>.</p>"}